<!--
  Status-bar / notification / quick-settings-tile icon.

  A white silhouette built 1:1 from the launcher icon's monochrome layer
  (res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_monochrome.xml — the briefcase + clock of
  the redesigned "Sykerö professor" app icon), re-scaled to fill the icon bounds
  (the adaptive-icon safe-zone padding of that layer renders far too small here).

  Two of the monochrome paths are used: the briefcase outline (which embeds the
  clock-face circle as a sub-path) plus the clock hand. fillType="evenOdd" turns
  the embedded circle into a cut-out so the clock reads as a face with a hand,
  rather than merging into a solid briefcase (the "Track Work Time" identity).

  Android renders small icons by their alpha mask and tints them, so a
  single-colour silhouette is required; the full-colour launcher icon cannot be
  used directly. Keep this in sync with the launcher monochrome layer if the app
  icon is redesigned again.
-->
